    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d8">

                <pb facs="0013" n="7" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg7"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">641.5531/19: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador to the Belgian Government in Exile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Biddle</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-13T13:00:00+02:00">May 13, 1942—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 13—8:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Belgian Series No. 8. My 3, April 30, 10 p.m. Vleeschauwer now plans to leave for
                    Congo via United States on May 15. He feels he cannot longer postpone departure
                    since this would dislocate his entire program.</p>
                <p>Joseph Jennen, Economic Adviser to Colonial Ministry, however has been given full
                    power to negotiate the United States-United Kingdom-Belgian Congo agreement.</p>
                <closer>[<signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Biddle</hi>
                    </signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
